From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:11:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bazel: build no Qt, drop qt-bazel from the module graph
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Bazel build's openroad links the gui's Qt-free core; its GUI is the
web viewer (//openroad/web). Qt was still in the module graph: MODULE.bazel
had bazel_dep(qt-bazel), which has no BCR version and resolves only
through a git_override in the root module, so every module that depends
on openroad had to repeat that override, and openroad/gui/BUILD loaded
@qt-bazel's build_defs.bzl at top level.

Removed: the qt-bazel bazel_dep and git_override; the freetype pin, the
icu override and its patch, and the macOS framework list, which exist
only for Qt; the gui_qt, gui_qt_headless, uic_lib and qt_resources
targets and the @qt-bazel load in openroad/gui; openroad-qt,
openroad_lib_qt, openroad_qt_build_test and the --//:platform=gui
branches (the flag keeps the value cli); the desktop entry the gui
platform installed; the gui tests that need a Qt build.

pcre2 is now a direct bazel_dep at 10.46-DEV, the version qt-bazel's
glib raised it to: swig asks for 10.43, whose BUILD overlay calls the
native cc_binary rule Bazel 9 removed.

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs; retires at a //:bump onto an
OpenROAD whose Bazel build makes Qt optional, so a module that depends
on openroad does not resolve qt-bazel.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
